|trivia =
*The [[Project Neural Cloud]] character [[Clukay]] is suspiciously similar to HK416.
*HK416 was the most [[Oath]]ed Doll during the first year of the game.<ref>[https://weibo.com/5611537367/F2LBOiAb9 First anniversary post on Weibo]</ref> She was eventually surpassed by {{doll name|M4A1|AR|4}}.
*<div class="spoiler">On the older servers, HK416 was the first 5* T-Doll to receive a Neural Upgrade, as well as the first ever T-Doll to achieve 6* rarity. This was not the case on the EN server, as NTW-20 received her neural upgrade first.</div>
*HK416 is the second T-Doll introduced who reloads her weapon as her victory sprite animation; the first one was {{doll name|Vector|SMG|5}}.
*The typical grenade launcher supplied to HK416 users is the AG36 (or M320). In the official manga, it is implied that HK416 stores her grenade launcher in the bag that she carries around with her.
**<div class="spoiler">Her modification stage 3 artwork has a M320 launcher depicted, and the chibi also uses said launcher to shoot grenades when she activates her skill.</div>
*HK416 was the rifle used to shoot and kill Osama Bin Laden. The SEAL Team operators used 5.56mm NATO 77-grain OTM (open-tip match) rounds made by Black Hills Ammunition.
**The code name "Geronimo" has been used in relation with the operation. The same name can be found in katakana (ジェロニモ) on 416's White Negroni costume, and is also referenced in Clukay's story event [[PNC Story/Divergent Shadows Nodes|Divergent Shadows]] in Project Neural Cloud.
*The collab exclusive costumes for {{doll name|HK416|AR|5|costume=costume5}}, {{doll name|Vector|SMG|5|costume=costume3}}, {{doll name|Agent 416|AR|EXTRA|costume=costume1}}, {{doll name|Agent Vector|SMG|EXTRA|costume=costume1}} can only be obtained via an in-game purchases using real money. Each costume can be found in Kalina's shop for 158 yuan.
*416 was one of the Dolls to be featured in the canceled game [[Girls' Frontline: Glitch Land]].
